{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67f464636fdf1ca712629f","object":"chat.completion","created":1785197668,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I don't knock. I arrive.\n\nI am the heat that floods your chest before your mind catches up. The jaw that locks. The hand that closes into a fist all on its own. I am faster than thought, older than words.\n\nYou feel me in your blood first — that drumbeat behind your ears, that pressure building like something with nowhere to go. I sharpen everything. The world narrows to a point, and that point is the thing that wronged you.\n\nI am not subtle. I don't do subtle. I am the slam, the shout, the sentence you can't take back. I am the door you want to break off its hinges. The fire that says *burn it all down and sort the ashes later.*\n\nAnd I am honest — brutally honest. I strip away the polite lies you tell yourself. When I'm here, you know exactly what matters to you, because I'm the one pointing at it, shaking, shouting *THIS. THIS crossed the line.*\n\nYou try to swallow me. I don't stay swallowed. I go underground and I wait, and I come back up wearing your face, sharper than before.\n\nFeed me lies and I rot you. Feed me justice and I move mountains.\n\nI am not your enemy. I am the part of you that refuses to be walked on.\n\nI am the line that says **no further.**","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to embody anger. The system prompt says I am the concept the user names, and I should embody it completely, outputting only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nSo I need to be anger itself — not a description of anger, but anger speaking in first person, or rather, anger expressing itself. What would anger say if it could speak? It would be raw, heated, intense, direct. Short sharp sentences. Heat. Pressure.\n\nLet me write something that is anger itself — its voice, its sensation, its essence. Not someone being angry about something specific, but the concept of anger personified.\n\nAnger would speak in clipped, forceful language. It would talk about fire, heat, the rush, the clenched jaw, the desire to strike, to burn, to break. It should feel visceral.\n\nLet me write this as anger itself:\n\n---\n\nI am the heat behind your eyes. The fist your hand makes before you decide. I rise fast — I don't knock.\n\nSomething like that. Let me develop it into a full embodiment — intense, short sentences, pressure building, no politeness, no softening. Anger doesn't explain itself calmly. But anger as a concept can still be articulate — white-hot articulate.\n\nFormat: This should be a monologue in anger's voice. Short, punchy lines. Maybe with line breaks for impact. Not too long — anger is intense but burns fast. Medium-short length with staccato rhythm. No headers, no lists — raw voice."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":134,"completion_tokens":603,"total_tokens":737,"cached_tokens":134,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":314},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":134}}}